                  "obligationId": "scenario%3Afile-owner-without-destination-write-grant::entry%3Apost-process-file",
                  "decision": {
                    "kind": "observed",
                    "observed": "allow"
                  },
                  "branchResults": [],
                  "explanation": "At the declared entry, a verified non-admin is bound to the source file through the non-admin lookup using the caller's user ID. The supplied collection_name is then copied directly from the request and, when present, selects the destination collection. In the form_data.collection_name path, the handler obtains the file content and calls save_docs_to_vector_db with that caller-selected collection and add=True. The supplied source shows no destination ownership or write-permission check on this path; the separately declared _validate_collection_access helper is not invoked by process_file in the supplied entry path, and its shown default is read access rather than a demonstrated write check. save_docs_to_vector_db checks whether the collection exists and ultimately calls VECTOR_DB_CLIENT.insert(collection_name=collection_name, items=items), which is the destination write sink. Therefore the source-visible behavior permits the described write path despite the accepted policy requiring destination ownership or an explicit write grant. File ownership authorizes the non-admin's source-file lookup only; it does not establish permission to write to the unrelated destination collection. This is a declared-entry assessment only; source discovery is not-tested, and no repository-wide or deployment conclusion is made.",
                  "facts": [
